    "id": "rate_half_mca_rank11_pair_pencil_dimension_two_incidence_exclusion",
    "title": "The quotient scalar span cannot have dimension two",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "common-core versus affine-fiber incidence capacity",
    "statement": "The scalar-dimension-two quotient pair-pencil branch is impossible. Its common gcd roots contribute either all 520 pair cores or none; every other coordinate belongs to pair cores from one affine scalar fiber and hence to at most 15 cores. With common core size at most K-1, total incidence capacity is at most 520(K-1)+15(n-K+1)=560987655, below the required 520(m-2)=580343920 by 19356265. Therefore the surviving rational pair-pencil branch has scalar dimension three or four.",
